      "text": "{\"id\":\"TIDY-473\",\"title\":\"Adopt DataFn field builders in the Nucleum schema\",\"description\":\"## Executive summary\\n\\nAdopt the published DataFn field-construction API from [DATA-2](<https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference>) in Nucleum's authoritative schema after the upstream implementation is released and available to this repository.\\n\\nReplace Nucleum's generic local primitive field factories with the DataFn-owned const-safe builders and named options. Preserve Nucleum-specific schema conventions and keep the effective runtime schema unchanged.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe current schema in `shared/data/datafn/schema.datafn.ts` defines local const-generic helpers for string, number, boolean, date, array, object, and JSON fields. They preserve the literals needed by `DatafnClient<typeof nucleumDatafnSchema>`, but duplicate framework typing logic and expose inconsistent positional argument ordering.\\n\\n<issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue> owns the upstream work:\\n\\n* public const-safe builders in `@datafn/core`;\\n* named, type-appropriate field options;\\n* literal enum and index safety;\\n* client nullability inference aligned with runtime defaults;\\n* documentation and compile-time coverage.\\n\\nThis issue is the downstream Nucleum adoption step. It is related to the broader [TIDY-442 DataFn migration](<https://linear.app/21n/issue/TIDY-442/datafn-migration-in-nucleum-playwright-tests-hardening>), but should remain separately reviewable from unrelated migration work.\\n\\n## Preconditions\\n\\n* <issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue> is complete.\\n* The exact DataFn version containing the field API and inference fixes is published or otherwise available through the repository's approved dependency path.\\n* The upstream API and its default semantics are documented and covered by DataFn tests.\\n* Nucleum's current effective schema can be captured for before/after comparison.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n* Update `shared/data/datafn/schema.datafn.ts` to import and use the released DataFn field builders.\\n* Convert positional calls to named options.\\n* Express enum fields through the supported upstream API without local object-spread workarounds where possible.\\n* Remove the replaced generic local primitive factory functions in the same change.\\n* Keep Nucleum product-specific composites and conventions local.\\n* Decide the local `idField` treatment according to <issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue>'s final published ID-field contract.\\n* Preserve resource names, field names, field kinds, requiredness, nullability, defaults, enums, uniqueness, capabilities, indices, permissions, relations, and schema version.\\n* Update dependency metadata only as required to consume the released DataFn version.\\n* Verify typed-client inference and the effective runtime schema after adoption.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n\\n* Implementing or backporting <issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue> inside Nucleum.\\n* Introducing compatibility wrappers, bridge APIs, or a second local field-builder layer.\\n* Changing persisted schema semantics or adding a data migration.\\n* Changing product behavior or user-facing UI.\\n* Moving `labelField`, `commonShareFields`, or other product-specific concepts into DataFn.\\n* Refactoring unrelated DataFn migration code covered by <issue id=\\\"6436318b-4f92-4b95-8efd-748b2566f053\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/TIDY-442/datafn-migration-in-nucleum-playwright-tests-hardening\\\">TIDY-442</issue>.\\n* Broad dependency upgrades unrelated to the released DataFn field API.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n* Nucleum consumes the released DataFn field-construction API from `@datafn/core`.\\n* The replaced local generic primitive factories are removed rather than retained as wrappers.\\n* Field definitions use named options and remain readable without positional boolean ambiguity.\\n* Literal field names, kinds, requiredness, nullability, defaults, and enum members remain preserved in the schema type.\\n* Compile-time index checking remains precise.\\n* The effective validated/normalized schema is equivalent before and after adoption, apart from any explicitly reviewed upstream normalization fix.\\n* No resource, relation, capability, index, permission, or persisted field contract changes unintentionally.\\n* Nucleum-specific composite fields remain local.\\n* The repository's relevant type-check, lint, schema/DataFn tests, and focused Nucleum checks pass.\\n* Any test changes follow repository policy; existing tests are not modified without explicit approval.\\n* Verification records the exact DataFn source/version consumed and distinguishes focused local checks from browser, CI, deployment, or production proof.\\n\\n## Dependencies and risks\\n\\n* Blocked by <issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue> and its released package/source availability.\\n* Related to <issue id=\\\"6436318b-4f92-4b95-8efd-748b2566f053\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/TIDY-442/datafn-migration-in-nucleum-playwright-tests-hardening\\\">TIDY-442</issue> because this schema is part of the ongoing Nucleum DataFn migration.\\n* The current checkout consumes several Superfunctions packages through local `file:` dependencies; adoption must use the approved dependency state for the target branch and CI.\\n* Builder defaults could alter serialized or normalized schema output if the upstream implementation differs from existing literals.\\n* Nullable/default behavior must be compared carefully because <issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue> includes an inference correction.\\n* An overly broad migration could mix library adoption with product schema changes and make review unsafe.\\n* Removing local helpers before the upstream version is actually consumable would break ordinary CI or registry-based builds.\\n\\n## Validation expectations\\n\\n* Capture the current schema output or normalized representation before editing.\\n* Compare effective field metadata and schema hashing/serialization after migration where supported.\\n* Run DataFn/Nucleum type checking that exercises `DatafnClient<typeof nucleumDatafnSchema>`.\\n* Run focused schema and DataFn tests relevant to the touched surface.\\n* Run repository lint/check commands appropriate to the final dependency state.\\n* Report any baseline failures separately.\\n* Treat local green checks as local evidence only; they do not establish browser, CI, deployment, or production behavior.\\n\\n## Open questions\\n\\n* What exact DataFn version and dependency form will Nucleum consume?\\n* Does the released API include `field.id()`, and if so, is its contract exactly equivalent to Nucleum's current ID field?\\n* Does <issue id=\\\"b80c565b-11ca-4d69-92ef-f5701b13384e\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-2/add-const-safe-field-builders-and-align-datafn-schema-inference\\\">DATA-2</issue> intentionally change the inferred type of any field whose `nullable` option is currently omitted?\\n* What is the canonical schema-equivalence or schema-hash check for this repository?\\n* Should adoption be one isolated schema/dependency change or part of a specifically approved <issue id=\\\"6436318b-4f92-4b95-8efd-748b2566f053\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/TIDY-442/datafn-migration-in-nucleum-playwright-tests-hardening\\\">TIDY-442</issue> stack segment?\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/TIDY-473/adopt-datafn-field-builders-in-the-nucleum-schema\",\"gitBranchName\":\"aravink/tidy-473-adopt-datafn-field-builders-in-the-nucleum-schema\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T12:55:40.845Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T12:55:41.948Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Aravind\",\"createdById\":\"3a6ed003-6380-47ef-9e7b-b2b01ebddc6a\",\"project\":\"Nucleum SF migration\",\"projectId\":\"013b7f72-1e10-434c-8db6-b3f19e5a15f8\",\"team\":\"Nucleum\",\"teamId\":\"454a22cf-025c-423f-9bcc-2b3142b47c62\"}"
    }
  ]
}

